WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:03.300
HanziFlow helps learners read real Chinese websites.

00:03.750 --> 00:05.000
Just highlight a sentence.

00:05.600 --> 00:09.050
The text is sent to a FastAPI server,
where a Qwen3 model,

00:09.050 --> 00:12.050
fine-tuned with QLoRA,
splits the sentence into words.

00:13.600 --> 00:16.450
We compared its output with Jieba, the standard tool.

00:19.550 --> 00:23.400
Here's the result: the full segmentation,
then every word on its own.

00:24.400 --> 00:25.950
Next, usage patterns.

00:26.450 --> 00:30.350
A Haystack RAG pipeline finds grammar structures
that match this sentence.

00:30.800 --> 00:35.100
Finally, a breakdown of the sentence pattern,
with pinyin and English for each part.

00:35.450 --> 00:36.850
No paid API needed.
